{
  "version": "v1",
  "description": "Telemetry consent as the `telemetry` capability. Reads: the grants file first, then the legacy record at kit.telemetry.consent in <XDG_CONFIG_HOME>/kit/config.yaml, then the legacy <XDG_CONFIG_HOME>/kit/telemetry.yaml (bare telemetry.consent). granted maps to allow, denied to deny, always with an empty subject. A telemetry write lands in the grants file, which is the source of truth from then on, and is mirrored into kit.telemetry.consent so SDKs that only read the legacy record keep the same answer. Revoke clears the grants file and both legacy records, other keys kept. The env precedence of the telemetry resolver still applies: KIT_TELEMETRY_MODE=off and DO_NOT_TRACK are a standing deny, KIT_TELEMETRY_CONSENT overrides the record. A corrupt grants file fails every check closed and is never repaired by a write, and config.yaml stays untouched.",
